From: Zach Taylor <zctaylor.work@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:35:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 14/30] Add an aws install profile with S3 snapshots and IRSA

A k0s cluster on AWS keeps snapshots in a real S3 bucket and gives atelet
and ate-api-server their AWS access through IRSA, so there is no static
key and no in-cluster rustfs. The profile layers on the k0s profile and
selects with ATE_INSTALL_PROFILE=aws. It drops the rustfs endpoint, path
style and key variables, sets the region and the role ARN annotations,
and has no GKE reference.

The gVisor SandboxConfig for the profile names runsc tarballs on your own
bucket. mirror-runsc.sh copies them from the public gvisor bucket after
it checks each hash, and it reads the releases and hashes from the
default SandboxConfig so the two cannot drift. validate.sh renders the
profile and checks it with kubeconform against the Substrate CRDs.

Fork-Topic: aws
Fork-Upstream: fork-only
